<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05KD">Example <span data-tag="05KD">7.6.6.31</span>.</a> Let $\mathbb {K}$ be a collection of simplicial sets. Then an $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ is $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="06BD" href="/tag/06BD">7.6.6.20</a>) if and only if the projection map $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \Delta ^0$ is a $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete inner fibration (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="05KC" href="/tag/05KC">7.6.6.28</a>). This is a special case of Example <a data-tag="05KH" href="/tag/05KH">7.6.6.30</a>, since $U$ is locally cartesian. </p>
